package gamemaker

const VoxelRuntimeGuide = `Voxel v1 uses startVoxelGame(definition,hooks) and src/voxel.json for its finite sandbox, grid collision and interactive targets.
Use base="voxel" and design.voxel as a JSON-encoded string in native set_design; schema 5 is server-owned. Choose survival (default) or creative from the request, fixed during play. Default size [96,48,96], maximum [128,64,128], multiples of 16. Terrain flat/hills/island, bounded seed. Read inspect.design_example for palette, items, recipes and enemies; preserve valid defaults. At most 64 block/item/recipe identities and 24 enemies. IDs/materials are storage identities. Plan acceptance and edits validate the same definition. Edit src/voxel.json using its current hash, then build/validate.
The authored world/rules definition is an implementation: keep concrete requested recipes, enemies and goals executable, not prose or renamed labels. Invented mechanics in features must be implemented with hooks. Optional goals use collect/craft/place with an item, or defeat without an item. No forced timer, combat or victory for peaceful sandboxes.
startVoxelGame(definition,{objective,setup(api),step(api,dtSeconds),action(api,target),dispose(api)}) owns the clock, mesh/physics, grid rays, resource/tool requirements, atomic inventory/crafting, enemies, start/pause, touch controls and persistence. action returning false suppresses the default mine/attack. Do not add another input/frame loop. main.ts imports definition from './voxel.json' and startVoxelGame from './common'.
api.getBlock(x,y,z), setBlock(x,y,z,id), transaction(take,give), count(item), craft(recipe), damagePlayer(amount), player/progress snapshots, scene,camera,renderer,event(name,point),dispose(). Only these APIs change the grid or inventory; never edit observations/counters. Scene decoration may use the existing model helper and must be disposed by the hook. World state, saves and chunk arrays never belong in prompts. Keep the 1m voxel scale and bounded first-person controls.
The intro precedes Start; compact status/hotbar during play. Desktop WASD/mouse/Space, primary mine/attack, secondary place, I inventory/crafting. E/F are accessible primary/secondary keyboard alternatives. Touch has a movement stick, look gesture and contextual actions. Inventory and pause freeze simulation. Studio saves use only the trusted host; do not add network or browser storage code. Exports already use IndexedDB.`
